The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says the reports are one issue with one fix queued. Its own
table shows more than one cause. Each cause in it now has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes the `parser` ticket only. The `hint` reports keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | in the table above | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` — day and month swapped | the `parser` row | [#1](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1) |
| `hint` — booking-v3 form asks month first | the `hint` row | [#2](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/2) |

The note under the table stays with the `parser` row: the desk files those reports under `parser`
by tenant, and so does [#1](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1).

## The two causes

**`parser` — day and month swapped.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Every
tenant on file writes the day first, so 3 May becomes 5 March. This is the fix that is queued.
Ticket [#1](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1).

**`hint` — the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order.** Under its date field, booking-v3
prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. People type month first, as the hint tells them, and the form reads the
tenant's way, day first. Only form reports from tenants on booking-v3. The parser fix does not
touch it: the form needs a day-first hint. The table marks it "no ticket of its own"; it has one
now: [#2](https://github.com/Yogelo/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/2).

**The one-day move note.** Some `parser` reports describe a date one day off, not a swap. The
desk noted them (`desk-notes.json`) and files them under `parser`; they are counted in #1, the
desk's way. Check them again once the parser fix ships.

## How the count was made

- The export repeats some rows. One id is one report.
- Cause by tenant and channel, as in `causes.ts`. `intakeTag` is not the cause: intake tags
  `hint` whenever the reporter's browser is `en-US`.
- A report is counted where the desk files it. Each ticket lists the report ids it covers.

## What changes on the desk

- Merging on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put both
  causes in one ticket, because their subjects match. Check the cause before you merge.
- Close #4471 against the parser fix only. Keep #2 open.

